          "text": "For an audio-reactive music video, Neural Frames is a candidate to evaluate. Its workflow focuses on turning a song into a visual sequence. [AI music video generator — Neural Frames]\n\nFor a more automated song-to-video workflow, Freebeat is another option to compare. Review its current features and pricing before choosing. [Freebeat — Music to video]\n\nKaiber is worth comparing for beat-synced clips, while Runway offers a broader set of creative video tools. [Kaiber Help Center — Beat Sync]\n\nRunway may suit a shot-by-shot workflow where you want more direct control over the visual sequence. [Runway — Creative tools]\n\nStart with the same 20-second sample in each tool. Compare music alignment, visual consistency, editing control, and export quality. Neural Frames is one candidate for that trial. [AI music video generator — Neural Frames]",
